      "sourceTextSha256": "44a05f12b66bcfcf244d4db5a0e4cd014e41f3345387fc7910f41630c83f29ec",
      "text": "A rose plantation (closed at weekends and on public holidays), then the Middle of the World: the Ciudad Mitad del Mundo, whose 30-metre monument stands about 240 m south of the true equator, and the Intiñán Museum, with experiments and displays on ancient cultures. In the afternoon, the Pululahua crater, one of the few inhabited volcanic craters in the world, where families farm corn and beans by hand on the crater floor, part of the Pululahua Geobotanical Reserve. Overnight at Hotel El Crater 4★. (B)",
